---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy: what Shapewell sees, and what it never does"
  description="Which behaviour signals Shapewell reads, where they live, what is never collected, and how Do Not Track and GPC are respected.">
  <section class="section privacy" aria-labelledby="pv-title">
    <div class="container pv">
      <header class="pv-head" data-slide="left">
        <div class="section-head"><span class="label"><span class="c">Privacy</span> / short and plain</span></div>
        <h1 id="pv-title" class="h-display">What Shapewell sees, <span class="accent">and what it never does.</span></h1>
        <p class="label label-sm"><span class="c">Last updated</span> / 16 October 2026</p>
      </header>

      <article class="pv-body">
        <section id="signals" data-slide="up">
          <h2 class="h-card">What it reads</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>How fast you scroll and how far down you get.</li>
            <li>How long sections are in view, and how long you rest the pointer on them (only after 1.2 seconds).</li>
            <li>Clicks and copy-button uses on those sections, and whether you use touch or a mouse.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>These are numbers about reading, not about you. You can watch every one of them live under "See why it changed".</p>
        </section>

        <section id="where" data-slide="up">
          <h2 class="h-card">Where it lives</h2>
          <p>
            In memory, in the tab you have open. Nothing is written to cookies or sent to a server, and it is gone when you
            close the tab.
          </p>
          <p>
            The only exception is something you choose to save with "Save this run" or "Save variant". That is kept in your
            browser's localStorage under <code>shapewell_runs</code>, on this device only. Delete it or download it as JSON
            from the "Saved" list under "See why it changed".
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="never" data-slide="up">
          <h2 class="h-card">What is never collected</h2>
          <p>
            Names, email addresses, IP-based location, device fingerprints or cross-site identifiers. The early access form
            on this demo does not send your email anywhere.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="control" data-slide="up">
          <h2 class="h-card">Your controls</h2>
          <p>
            If your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, adapting is paused by default. Open "See why it
            changed" to pause adapting, reset the page to its default shape, or turn adapting back on.
          </p>
          <p>Questions: <a class="link" href="mailto:privacy@shapewell.dev">privacy@shapewell.dev</a>.</p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .pv {
    display: grid;
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .pv-head {
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .pv-head .section-head {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .pv-head h1 {
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .pv-body {
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .pv-body section {
    padding: 28px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .pv-body h2 {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .pv-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 1em;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .pv-body li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--f-mono);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
</style>
